@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-logical-functions Logical Functions
@brief Functions used to compose logical expressions in tests.

@details
The functions `mt::both()`, `mt::either()`, and `mt::negate()` combine
multiple conditions, allowing expressive and concise test logic.
`mt::either()` is an inclusive or: it is true also when both conditions
are true.

The functions have descriptive names, since `and`, `or`, and `not` are
alternative tokens and cannot be used as identifiers. Using these logical
functions allows developers to express compound conditions clearly and
improve readability.

@par Example

@code{.cpp}
ts.test ("Check compound conditions", [] (auto& t) {
  t.expect (mt::both (mt::eq (compute_answer (), 42),
                      mt::eq (compute_float (), 42.0)));
});
@endcode

The overloaded logical operators of the `micro_test_plus::operators`
namespace are deprecated since 5.1.0, in favour of these functions.
